+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -209,6 +209,11 @@ equivalent:
 
 ## Go-to-Definition Architecture
 
+Member navigation uses the shared subject resolver's candidate classes and keeps
+one valid declaration per candidate, preserving each candidate's trait/framework
+fallback order. Identical inherited declarations are deduplicated; multiple
+concrete declarations are returned to the client as alternatives.
+
 The definition subsystem uses a **three-tier** approach, from fastest to slowest:
 
 ### Tier 1: Precomputed Symbol Map (primary)
